---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Contact from "../components/Contact.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms for playing Draigon Idle and using draigonidle.com."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>Last updated: {site.legalUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        These terms cover the {site.name} app (the "game") and the website at
        draigonidle.com (the "site"). The game is made by {site.person}, an independent
        developer publishing as {site.studio} ("we", "us"). By playing the game or
        using the site, you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Playing the game</h2>
      <p>
        We give you a personal, non-transferable licence to install and play the game
        on Apple devices you own or control, as Apple's App Store rules allow. The game
        is licensed to you, not sold. Apple's standard
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" rel="noopener">Licensed Application End User Licence Agreement</a>
        also applies to the app.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Age</h2>
      <p>
        You need to be at least 13 to use the game or the site. If you're under the age
        of majority where you live, a parent or guardian needs to agree to these terms
        for you.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The purchase</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The game is free to start. One optional purchase opens the rest of it.</li>
        <li>
          It's a one-time purchase, not a subscription. It belongs to the Apple account
          that bought it and can be restored on your other devices from the game's
          Settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          Apple takes the payment and sets the price in your currency. Refunds are
          handled by Apple, under Apple's refund rules. We can't issue them ourselves.
        </li>
        <li>There are no other purchases, and nothing in the game can be bought with real money beyond this.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Your save</h2>
      <p>
        Your progress is stored only on your device. We don't hold a copy and can't
        restore one. Deleting the app deletes the save, although your purchase can
        always be restored.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Beta versions</h2>
      <p>
        Test versions are unfinished. They may have bugs, their balance may change, and
        a save from a test version may be reset. Feedback you send us may be used to
        improve the game without payment or credit, though we're grateful for it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Fair use</h2>
      <p>Please don't:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>copy, resell or redistribute the game or its art, music and writing;</li>
        <li>get round the purchase or tamper with the game to unlock paid content;</li>
        <li>use the game or the site for anything unlawful, or to harm other people;</li>
        <li>attack, overload or scrape the site in a way that disrupts it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The game, its name, art, sound, writing and code belong to {site.person}.
        Sharing screenshots and videos of your own play is welcome, including in
        monetised videos and streams.
      </p>

      <h2>8. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The game and the site are provided as they are. We work to keep them running
        well, but to the extent the law allows we don't promise they will be free of
        errors or always available. Nothing here limits rights you have under consumer
        law that can't be limited.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Limit of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, we aren't liable for indirect or consequential
        losses from using the game or the site, including lost game progress, and our
        total liability to you is limited to what you paid for the game.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the game changes. The date at the top shows the
        latest version. Carrying on playing after a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the place where the developer lives,
        without regard to its conflict-of-law rules, except where the consumer law of
        your own country gives you rights that can't be set aside.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: reach us at <Contact />.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
